<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zheng Zhilong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1604">1604</a>–<a href="/years/1661">1661</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Nicholas Iquan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zheng Zhilong was a Chinese merchant and pirate who built a great maritime trading network from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a>. He entered Ming service as an admiral, supported the Ming loyalist court in Fujian, then surrendered to the Qing in 1646. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koxinga">Koxinga</a> continued the resistance, and the Qing executed Zheng Zhilong in 1661.</p></div>
